                <pb facs="0368" n="286" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg286"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/625.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic">August 5,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Knox instructs Mr. Furniss, in reply to his August 4, to caution American
                    citizens to observe a strictly neutral attitude and to refrain from all
                    participation in political matters. Telegraphic instructions are being sent to
                    the commanding officer at Port au Prince.</p>
            </div>
